    {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::activity_event_contract_copied",
      "confidence": "high",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "summary": "ActivityEvent is defined four times per agent and a fifth time inline without workflow_run_id",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "abstraction_fitness",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/triage-agent/src/activity.rs",
          "crates/detection-agent/src/activity.rs",
          "crates/response-agent/src/activity.rs",
          "crates/hunt-agent/src/activity.rs",
          "crates/vuln-agent/src/main.rs",
          "crates/agent-protocol/src/lib.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "The four activity.rs files differ only in doc comments and in `step: &'static str` (triage) vs `step: String` (the other three); each also re-declares SUBJECT_ACTIVITY = \"ares.activity\" and an identical emit() helper in main.rs",
          "vuln-agent emits a bare json!({agent, step, detail, ts}) (crates/vuln-agent/src/main.rs:120-135) with no workflow_run_id, while docs/services.md specifies {workflow_run_id, agent, step, detail, ts} and both SSE filters key on workflow_run_id (api-server/src/a2a.rs:600, acp.rs:560)",
          "agent-protocol already owns the other NATS subjects (SUBJECT_ALERTS..SUBJECT_BAS) but not SUBJECT_ACTIVITY, so the console contract has no single definition"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Move ActivityEvent and SUBJECT_ACTIVITY into agent-protocol (next to the other subjects), delete the four activity.rs copies and the five emit() helpers, and have vuln-agent construct the same struct so its events carry workflow_run_id.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "62b3ecc9"
      },
